Source: pccl
Section: libs
Maintainer: sail.support <sail.support@thead.com>
Priority: optional
Build-depends: debhelper(>=9)
Standards-Version: 3.9.5

Package: libpccl${pccl:Major}
Section: libs
Architecture: ${pkg:Arch}
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: PPU Collective Communication Library (PCCL) Runtime
 PCCL (pronounced "Pickle") is the PPU Collective Communication Library,
 providing high-performance collective and point-to-point communication for
 PPU accelerators. It supports all-reduce, all-gather, reduce-scatter, reduce,
 broadcast, all-to-all, gather, scatter, and send/receive operations for
 distributed deep learning and HPC workloads.
 It has been optimized to achieve high bandwidth on Zhenwu PPU hardware using
 PCIe, ICNLink, ICNSwitch, as well as RDMA networks or TCP/IP sockets.

Package: libpccl-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: ${pkg:Arch}
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, libpccl${pccl:Major} (= ${binary:Version})
Description: PPU Collective Communication Library (PCCL) Development Files
 PCCL (pronounced "Pickle") is the PPU Collective Communication Library,
 providing high-performance collective and point-to-point communication for
 PPU accelerators. It supports all-reduce, all-gather, reduce-scatter, reduce,
 broadcast, all-to-all, gather, scatter, and send/receive operations for
 distributed deep learning and HPC workloads.
 This package contains header files and static libraries for development.
